# AGENTS.md

Instructions for coding agents working on `[[ project_name ]]`. Full detail
for humans is in [README.md](README.md) and [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Layout

- Package code: `src/[[ package_name ]]/`. CLI entry point:
  `src/[[ package_name ]]/cli.py`.
- Unit tests: `tests/unit/` (the default `pytest` run).
- Integration tests: `tests/integration/`, marked `integration`, talking to
  real services; they skip unless `RUN_INTEGRATION=1` is set.
- Python [[ python_version ]] only (`.python-version`); dependencies are
  managed with uv (`pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`).

## Commands

```bash
uv sync                               # install dependencies
uv run pytest                         # unit tests
uv run ruff format .                  # format
uv run ruff check --fix .             # lint
uv run pre-commit run --all-files     # secrets, SAST, workflow lint/audit
uv add <package>                      # add a dependency (--dev for tooling)
```

Run tests, format, and lint before finishing a change. Don't edit `uv.lock`
by hand; use `uv add`, `uv remove`, or `uv lock`.
[%- if flavor == 'browser' %]

## Browser automation

The project drives Chromium with Playwright; `src/[[ package_name ]]/browser.py`
has `open_page()` and `pause()`.

```bash
uv run playwright install --with-deps chromium   # once, if the browser is missing
uv run pytest --headed --slowmo 500              # watch the browser tests
uv run playwright show-trace <file.zip>          # replay a recorded run
```

- Run headless (`headless=True`, `--headless`) yourself; headed runs need a
  display and are for the developer to watch.
- Browser tests build their own pages (`page.set_content`); don't make tests
  depend on a live site.
- Use Playwright's own sync API from one place per process: pytest-playwright's
  fixtures hold it during tests, so test CLI runs in a subprocess.
- Prefer role- and text-based locators (`get_by_role`, `get_by_text`) over CSS
  selectors, and Playwright's auto-waiting over sleeps.
[%- endif %]

## Conventions

- Pull request titles follow
  [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)
  (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, ...): PRs are squash-merged, so the title sets
  the version bump and changelog entry.
- Don't bump the version or edit `CHANGELOG.md`; release-please does both.
- Pin GitHub Actions and pre-commit hook revs to full commit SHAs with the
  version in a trailing comment; Dependabot updates them.
- Don't suppress a security finding (Betterleaks, Semgrep, zizmor, Trivy)
  without confirming it's a false positive; suppress narrowly, with a comment
  saying why (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
- Configuration and secrets come from environment variables only; locally,
  the git-ignored `.env` holds them. Never put secrets in other files (no key
  or credential files), and never read, create, or commit `.env`.
- `.env.example` lists every environment variable the application reads at
  run time. When code starts reading a new one, add it there in the same
  change, with a comment saying what it's for and a placeholder value, never
  a real one. Development and test switches (e.g. `RUN_INTEGRATION`) don't
  go in it.
- `.copier-answers.yml` is managed by Copier; don't edit it. Template updates
  come in with `uvx copier update --trust`.
